.TH SYS_YIELD 2
.SH NAME
sys_yield \- let another thread run (SYS_YIELD)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include "mk.h"

long sys_yield(void);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sys_yield
gives the processor to another ready thread, if there is one. The calling
thread stays ready: it goes to the back of its processor's run queue and
runs again in its turn.
.PP
Waiting for something is better done with a call that sleeps until it
happens
.RB ( ipc_recv (2),
.BR sys_futex (2),
.BR sys_sleep (2)):
a loop around
.B sys_yield
keeps a processor busy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Always 0.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sys_sleep (2),
.BR sys_place (2),
.BR intro (2)
